{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If he has not put forth his hand.</b> Indicates that ונקרב בעל הבית שבועה ('and the householder shall approach' — the oath) is according to the judges; therefore after it, על כל דבר פשע שפשע הנשבע ('for every matter of negligence that the oath-taker negligenced'). And Rabbi Yeshuah said: פשע means that which went out of his domain, as in אז תפשע אדום מתחת יד יהודה ('then Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah,' 2 Kings 8:22). And so על כל דבר פשע includes what comes after it and every matter that went out of the owner's domain — whether stolen, whether lost and he denied it and did not acknowledge it."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:19.771289807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}